<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Smurfit Corp Q4 net income drops to $14mln.</title>
<headline>Smurfit Corp Q4 net income drops to $14mln.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million $ unless stated)</p>
<p> Net income		    14.0		   vs 64.0</p>
<p> Net income p/shr(cents)   0.13		   vs 0.57</p>
<p> Net sales		     816.0		  vs 973.0</p>
<p>Income from operations    75.0		   vs 154.0</p>
<p>Interest expense	    47.0		   vs 53.0</p>
<p>Income before tax and</p>
<p>    extraordinary item    25.0		   vs 106.0</p>
<p>Provision for income tax  10.0 charge	  vs 41.0 charge</p>
<p>Extraordinary charge	1.0		    vs 1.0</p>
<p>Note: Jefferson Smurfit Corp, a U.S. unit of Ireland's Jefferson Smurfit Group, said the extraordinary charge of $1.0 million was a loss from early extinguishment of debt, net of income tax benefits.  </p>
<p>				 Results for 12 months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>Net income		    112.0		  vs 243.0</p>
<p>Net income p/shr(cents)   1.01		   vs 2.19</p>
<p>Net sales		     3,410.0		vs 4,093.0</p>
<p>Income from operations    391.0		  vs 630.0</p>
<p>Interest expense	    194.0		  vs 234.0</p>
<p>Income before tax and</p>
<p>    extraordinary item    194.0		  vs 403.0</p>
<p>Provision for income tax  77.0 charge	  vs 156.0 charge</p>
<p>Extraordinary charge	5.0		    vs 4.0</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
